					<h1 class="title" title="Amethi Tour">Amethi Tour</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">
<h3>Amethi Tour - World Fame Parliamentary Constituency</h3>
<p><b>Amethi</b> is located at the south-west part of <b>Sultanpur district</b> in <b>Uttar Pradesh, India</b>. It 
officially comes under the <b>Chhatrapati Shahuji Maharaj Nagar district</b>, which is the newest and 72nd district of 
the state of Uttar Pradesh. This district is part of <b>Faizabad</b> division. It is named after Chhatrapati Shahuji 
Maharaj, a <b>social reformer in Maharashtra</b>.Amethi is very well known in the <b>Indian Political history</b> as the seat of power of the Nehru-Gandhi political 
dynasty.</p>
 <p>The total <b>Rural Population of Amethi</b> is 83299 and the literacy rate is 39.5%.</p>

<h3>How to reach here:</h3>
<p>Amethi is well connected to all <b>major cities in Uttar Pradesh</b> and <b>North-Eastern India</b> via <b>Indian Railways</b> and 
roads. It has many direct trains connecting with major cities like <b>Delhi, Lucknow, Kanpur, Dehradun, Haridwar, Allahabad, Varanasi, Kolkata, Puri</b> and 
many more. A number of <b>Uttar Pradesh State Road Transport Corporation</b> buses ply from Amethi, providing seamless 
local and national connectivity.</p>

<p>The closest major airport is <b>Amausi Airport</b> (141 km). This airport has international and domestic flights 
from <b>Lucknow</b>.</p>

<h3>Political Background</h3>
<p>The <b>Amethi Parliamentary Constituency</b> is a world fame seat mainly due to being connected with first Prime 
Minister and architect of <b>modern India Shri Jawahar Lal Nehru's family</b>. Both the sons of former Prime Minister 
<b>Smt. Indira Gandhi, Shri Sanjay Gandhi</b> and thereafter <b>Shri Rajiv Gandhi</b>, who became <b>Prime Minister of India</b>, 
represented this constituency. Now it is represented by <b>Smt. Sonia Gandhi</b>, the wife of late Shri Rajiv Gandhi 
and presently the <b>President of Indian National Congress</b> as well as the leader of opposition in <b>Indian Parliament</b>.</p> 

<h3>Health & Education</h3>
<p>Amethi has well known hospital known as <b>Sanjay Gandhi Hospital</b> at Munshiganj. Society for Animal Health 
Agriculture Science and Humanity is well known non-government organisation whose registered office is located at 
<b>Munshiganj</b> which is dedicated for transformation of rural life in Amethi. As an educational hub of the area 
it has got Indian Institute of Information Technology and Rajarshi Rananjay Post Graduate College.</p>

<h3>Places of interest</h3>
<p>Amethi, located at the south-west part of Sultanpur may boast of having the Avionics Division of Hindustan 
Aeronautics Limited, the organisation is responsible for manufacture of Aircraft for <b>Indian Airforce</b>. Amethi has also a 
unit of Indo Gulf Fertilizers.</p> 
<p>Amethi is also called as <b>Raipur-Amethi</b> of which Raipur belonged to the Raja of Amethi who lived at 
Ram Nagar. There is a temple called Hanumangarhi and a mosque both built about hundred years ago. About 3 km north of 
Ram Nagar there is a tomb of famous poet, Saint Malik Muhammad Jaisi where he died, and the fort was built by 
Bachghoti Rajas.</p>


